# TelltaleLocalizationTool — Simple License

**Short version:** Use it freely. If you make money with it, give credit. Donations are optional.

## What you can do

You can use, copy, modify, and share TelltaleLocalizationTool for personal or commercial work.

## Credit for commercial use

If you use this tool to make or provide a commercial translation, mod, asset, or service, please credit it to your customers.

For public sales or downloads, put the credit on your sales/download page — **or preferably show the ByteAndPlay logo/image at the start of the game (splash screen).**

For private client work without a public listing, include the credit in the written handoff.

Use this credit text:

> Created using TelltaleLocalizationTool by ByteAndPlay.  
> https://github.com/MRJAPPS/TelltaleLocalizationTool

That’s it — just let people know the tool helped you.

## Redistribution

If you share the source or binaries, keep this license and the existing copyright/attribution notices. If you modified it, make that clear. You can claim credit for your own changes, but not for the original project or other contributors’ work.

## Your work stays yours

Your translations and other original output belong to you. You don’t have to publish them. This license doesn’t give you rights to game files, fonts, external tools, or other third-party material — check those licenses yourself.

## Donations

Donations are completely optional. No donation, royalty, or share of sales is required. If you feel like supporting the project, thank you — it’s appreciated.

## No warranty

The tool is provided “as is,” without warranty of any kind. Use it at your own risk.

